#pragma once
#include <vector>

#include "core/profile_series.h"

namespace cc::core {

/// Series and profiles of the "Describir" dialog transcribed from the user's manual captures of the original
/// (docs/research/ui/describir_barras_capturas_manuales.md). The data is generated by tools/gen_describir_data.py from the TSV
/// files of docs/research/ui/data/ (never typed by hand).
///
/// What the captures give is the designation of each profile ("IPC 533x203x62.6", "UF-60x3", "S-100x100"...), and only those
/// numbers are stored (see the shapes of section_properties.h):
///  - Timber (round, square, rectangular, variable depth): fully calculable. "S-NxB" / "GL-AxB" are depth x width as the series
///    names ("Maciza hN", "Laminada bB") say; the order of "Cabios/Viguetas" (100x70) follows by analogy (NOT verified). The
///    variable-depth series RV-60..RV-260 store the width; the initial / final depths are the 100.0 mm defaults of the dialog
///    ("Canto del perfil") and are edited per bar. The full name of that series was not visible (truncated in the capture): the clone
///    uses the name of the shape, "Rectangular, canto variable" (TODO(captura)).
///  - Built-up (IPC), cold-formed (U, C) and aluminium ((EP) I): the designation alone does not give the thicknesses, so their
///    mechanical properties are NOT calculable (TK-052); the library accepts them, describing a bar with them is refused.
///  - Ties (five shapes): kept apart from the library because their series "L" would collide with the library series "L" of the
///    rolled angles (series references are unique). The radii of the angles are 0 (not given by the designation, PROVISIONAL) and the
///    orientation of "FL b x t" is the order of the designation (PROVISIONAL).

/// Series of the library in the order of the captures: IPC (armado), U and C (conformado), (EP) I (aluminio), then the timber series
/// (Redondo; Maciza, DUO/TRIO, Laminada; Cabios/Viguetas, Maciza hN, DUO/TRIO hN, Laminada bB; Rectangular, canto variable).
const std::vector<ProfileSeries>& describirSeries();

/// predefinedSeries() followed by describirSeries(): what "Importar series de perfiles predefinidas" and the Describir dialog offer.
const std::vector<ProfileSeries>& importablePredefinedSeries();

/// The tie series of a tie shape (AngleEqual "L", AngleUnequal "L", FlatBar "Pletinas", RoundBar "R", SquareBar "Barras cuadradas"),
/// or nullptr. The profiles are not part of any library.
const ProfileSeries* tieSeries(ShapeKind shape);
/// The five tie shapes in the order of the original's icons (Angular simétrico, Angular, Platabanda, Redondo macizo, Cuadrado macizo).
const std::vector<ShapeKind>& tieShapes();

}  // namespace cc::core
